! The hydrogen chain of h-chain-spiral-elk.in, DOUBLED along z and run collinear:
! the antiferromagnet, the two moments opposite.
!
! This pair is the arbiter for the factor of five between this code's E(q) and
! Elk's. Both codes compute a spiral through their own implementation of the
! generalized Bloch theorem, so a disagreement about E(q) could be the machinery
! or the physics, and nothing separated the two. This cell contains no spiral at
! all: q = b3/2 of the unit cell **is** the collinear antiferromagnet of the cell
! doubled along z, which is a statement about the two states rather than about
! either code, so
!
!     E(AFM) - E(FM) in the doubled cell = 2 [ E(q = 1/2) - E(q = 0) ]
!
! and both sides can be had from ordinary collinear runs.
!
! This code's own spiral already satisfies that identity to **1e-10 Ry**
! (tests/regression/test_spin_spirals.py's q = b3/2 test, whose reference has
! nspin = 2 and is not a spiral at all), so this pair is not a check of defumat
! against itself -- it is the number Elk's collinear path can be asked for, on a
! cell where Elk's spiral is not involved.
!
! Everything else is the spiral fixture's so that the two runs differ by the cell
! and the magnetic arrangement and by nothing else: the functional (input_dft =
! 'pw', matching Elk's xctype = 3), the dataset, the cutoff, the smearing and the
! convergence threshold. The k-grid is 1 1 4 because the cell is twice as long,
! which samples the same Brillouin zone as the unit cell's 1 1 8 -- the grid the
! defumat scan converged at.
!
! The two atoms are two species pointing at one file, which is what lets a
! starting magnetization differ between them in a way pw.x can also read.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 0.83333333333333,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    input_dft = 'pw'
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10
    nspin = 2
    nosym = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6
    starting_magnetization(2) = -0.6
    nbnd = 12
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
    electron_maxstep = 300
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H1 1.008 H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H2 1.008 H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.0
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.5
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 4 0 0 0
